    "id": "journaling",
    "title": "Recognise, reflect, redirect",
    "accent": "reflect, redirect.",
    "group": "The core of the comfort",
    "summary": "Two journaling exercises, with space to respond to each of six prompts.",
    "journal": true,
    "sourceEdition": true,
    "sections": [
      {
        "title": "Recognise, reflect, redirect",
        "label": "",
        "body": '<p>CHAPTER 01 the nurturing system of Almighty Allah JOURNALING PROMPTS HOW DOES THE WORD MAKTH ( \u0645\u0643\u062B ), REMAINING FOR A LIMITED TIME, CHALLENGE MY DESIRE TO CREATE ABADIYYAH ( \u0623\u0628\u062F\u064A\u0629 ), PERMANENCE, IN THIS WORLDLY LIFE?</p><p>Recognising:Where in my life am I trying to make something last forever (a relationship, a possession, a status, a comfort) even though my stay in this world is only makth?</p><p>Reflecting: If true abadiyyah belongs only to the Hereafter ( \u0645\u0627\u0643\u062B\u064A\u0646 \u0641\u064A\u0647 \u0623\u0628\u062F\u0627 ), how does that change the way I hold on to what I have now?</p><p>Redirecting: How can I turn my natural longing for permanence toward what truly lasts: al-b\u0101qiy\u0101t al-\u1E63\u0101li\u1E25\u0101t, sincere deeds, beneficial knowledge, and righteous children?</p><p>CHAPTER 01 the nurturing system of Almighty Allah JOURNALING PROMPTS WHY IS THE BASH\u0100RAH ( \u0628\u0634\u0627\u0631\u0629 ) PROMISED FOR MY \u02BFIB\u0100DAH SUCH A SOLACE WHEN I FEEL I CANNOT GO ON?</p><p>Recognising: When was the last time I felt I could not go on?</p><p>Which act of \u02BFib\u0101dah held me up in that moment, even a little?</p><p>*Reflecting: The bish\u0101rah in S\u016Brat al-Kahf is for</p><blockquote><p class="arabic-text" lang="ar" dir="rtl">\u0627\u0644\u0645\u0624\u0645\u0646\u064A\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0630\u064A\u0646 \u064A\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0648\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0635\u0627\u0644\u062D\u0627\u062A</p><p>, those who believe and do righteous deeds (18:2). How does knowing that my effort is seen and rewarded, even when no one else notices, change how I carry my difficulty?</p></blockquote><p>Redirecting:Bish\u0101rah is news that shows on the face. How can I let this glad tidings show in my life and in how I speak to myself in hard moments, so that hope is my first response instead of despair?</p>'
      },
      {
        "title": "Summary & connections",
        "label": "OPTIONAL ASIDE",
        "body": '<details class="course-summary-aside"><summary>Lesson summary</summary><p>Two journaling exercises, with space to respond to each of six prompts.</p></details>'
      },
      {
        "title": "Pause & reflect",
        "label": "PERSONAL REFLECTION",
        "body": '<div class="journal-question"><label><strong>RECOGNISING Where in my life am I trying to make something last forever \u2014 a relationship, a possession, a status, a comfort \u2014 even though my stay in this world is only makth?</strong></label><textarea data-note-key="makth-recognising"></textarea></div><div class="journal-question"><label><strong>REFLECTING If true abadiyyah belongs only to the Hereafter (\u0645\u0627\u0643\u062B\u064A\u0646 \u0641\u064A\u0647 \u0623\u0628\u062F\u064B\u0627), how does that change the way I hold on to what I have now?</strong></label><textarea data-note-key="makth-reflecting"></textarea></div><div class="journal-question"><label><strong>REDIRECTING How can I turn my natural longing for permanence toward what truly lasts: al-b\u0101qiy\u0101t al-s\u0101li\u1E25\u0101t, sincere deeds, beneficial knowledge, and righteous children?</strong></label><textarea data-note-key="makth-redirecting"></textarea></div><div class="journal-question"><label><strong>RECOGNISING When was the last time I felt I could not go on? Which act of \u2018ib\u0101dah held me up in that moment, even a little?</strong></label><textarea data-note-key="bisharah-recognising"></textarea></div><div class="journal-question"><label><strong>REFLECTING The bish\u0101rah in Surah al-Kahf is for \u0627\u0644\u0645\u0624\u0645\u0646\u064A\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0630\u064A\u0646 \u064A\u0639\u0645\u0644\u0648\u0646 \u0627\u0644\u0635\u0627\u0644\u062D\u0627\u062A, those who believe and do righteous deeds (18:2). How does knowing that my effort is seen and rewarded, even when no one else notices, change how I carry my difficulty?</strong></label><textarea data-note-key="bisharah-reflecting"></textarea></div><div class="journal-question"><label><strong>REDIRECTING Bish\u0101rah is news that shows on the face. How can I let these glad tidings show in my life and in how I speak to myself in hard moments, so that hope is my first response instead of despair?</strong></label><textarea data-note-key="bisharah-redirecting"></textarea></div>'
      }
    ]
